One of the most asked Kubernetes questions is CrashLoopBackOff

Here's how you should answer it

CrashLoopBackOff happens when your container repeatedly exits after starting many times. 

It may happen because of a config issue, a wrong template, a poor container, or incorrect secrets or variables

How to troubleshoot it?
→ Check the logs of the pod
→ Describe the pod to know what is happening
→ Recheck env variables and secrets
→ Configuration setup
→ Liveness and Readiness Probles
→ Dependency on other Pods

You can use this to find the root cause one by one and fix the issue.

It helped me fix this issue multiple times. It will work for you as well.
